owner_conformance:
The owner decision was read verbatim (Dutch, both messages; message 2 takes precedence), as was the futuristic ambition of 14 November 2026.

**Needs.** All eight named need groups have matrix rows and a research section with Q1–Q6 answered:
- colour vision: rows 1–5, section 3.1;
- low vision, blindness and magnification: rows 6–18, sections 3.2–3.3;
- light sensitivity and migraine: rows 19–23, section 3.4;
- photosensitive epilepsy, vestibular and motion: rows 24–32, sections 3.5–3.6;
- dyslexia, dyscalculia and other learning differences: rows 34–43, sections 3.7–3.8 and 3.12;
- ADHD, autism and other cognitive or sensory needs: rows 44–53, sections 3.9–3.11;
- motor and alternative input: rows 57–74, section 3.13;
- hearing: rows 75–81, section 3.14.

**Additions.** The categories were extended as the owner asked: stereoscopic depth, memory and acquired brain injury, plain language, speech, and deafblindness and braille (sections 3.11, 3.12, 3.15, 3.16), each with Q1–Q6.

**Dyslexia and dyscalculia.** Alternatives were studied: read-aloud, paired text spacing, line length, a reading ruler, and numeric aids that never remove the exact value. Dyslexia fonts are rejected and graded contradicted, with no cure claims.

**Medical claims.** No unproven medical claim was found. Tint, overlays, blue light, correcting glasses and dyslexia fonts are explicitly claim-free, and section 6.1 makes 'no setting claims to treat or cure' a baseline rule.

**Extensions.** They are recorded separately: section 10.1 lists 8 extensions of existing contracts and section 10.2 lists 8 new contracts. No contract file changed.

**Matrix columns.** The matrix has 12 columns covering need, barrier, adaptation, tier, configuration, normative basis, evidence grade, sources, prototype status, native status, verification method and user test. These cover every element the owner listed. The exact required column list was not given to this verifier, so the matrix was judged against the owner text.

**Two tiers (message 2), both directions.**
- Every safety limit is baseline and none depends on a manual setting. This includes the vestibular limit at boot, before any preference exists.
- Device preferences start the settings automatically.
- The default is protected from dulling: rich only adds intensity, every flagship identity feature is in the regular default, light, opacity and colour stay free under the vestibular limit, and the 1400 ms boot convergence is kept as a convergence of light.
- No diagnosis profiles; presets are named combinations of axes only.

check_py:
